=== How to use ===
1. Host the API on HTTPS without authentication, or put it behind Azure API Management with a public read-only product.
2. Reference the plugin from your declarative agent, then sideload and try the two conversation starters.
3. Choose ShowUsageWithInput while you test so that you can see what Copilot sends; switch to ShowUsage if the input could contain sensitive text.
4. Add rate limiting on the API side, because anonymous endpoints can be called by any user of the agent.
5. When you later add private data, change the runtime auth and move the affected functions to GetPrivateData.

=== Common mistakes ===
- Using auth type none in lowercase. The documented value is None.
- Sending personal data to an anonymous endpoint just because it is convenient. GetPublicData is only correct if the call returns unauthenticated external data.
- Forgetting to explain the country code format in the parameter description, which leads to values such as Germany instead of DE.
- Leaving out year handling: models often guess the current year unless the description says that year is required.
- Declaring the office function without a 404 response; the model then cannot explain an unknown office.

